  "summary": "Transport your senses to the coastal shores of Kerala with this fragrant Indian soup that features <b>a rich seafood profile</b>. Succulent wild prawns simmer gently in an aromatic broth made from freshly extracted coconut milk, tangy tamarind paste, and tempered mustard seeds. A signature base of fried curry leaves, crushed shallots, and ginger-garlic paste imparts an earthy warmth that balances the natural sweetness of the fresh shellfish. Turmeric and green chilies provide a vibrant golden color alongside a gentle spicy kick that lingers delightfully on the palate. Designed to highlight delicate ocean flavors, the prawns are added at the very end of cooking to preserve their succulent, tender texture. Pair this luscious coastal soup with steamed basmati rice or crusty bread to soak up every drop of spiced coconut broth. It offers an extraordinary balance of tropical creaminess and coastal spice.",
